# The glass shadows scene (see docs/rendering/global-illumination.md#many-lights): three closed white corridors side by
# side, each lit only by a point light in a black box behind a window in its south wall. The first window is deep red
# glass, which casts shadows, the second is open, and the third is a white panel. The global illumination's rays see
# through a window of glass alone into the black box, which gives them nothing, so the corridor's light reaches them
# only through their hits' shadow rays toward the light, which pass through the glass dimmed and tinted by its
# transmittance. Compare the Gi_Diffuse view in each corridor from (x - 1.1, 1.5, 0.5) facing the south wall beside its
# window, x being -4, 0 and 4, where neither the window nor a lit surface is on the screen: red and dim behind the
# glass, white behind the open window, dark behind the panel, at one manual exposure and no ambient light. Positions are raw World_Position
# values in units of 2^-24 m. The editor writes this file; see docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
